{"build":"3f725a0@18/11/2026, 19:55:55","data":{"book":{"title":"Kirtan Guide","title_full_short":"Kīrtan Guide 12th Ed","subtitle":"London, Twelfth Edition, 2026","slug":"en","sort_order":1,"shortcuts":[{"icon":"clock","title":"The Daily Programme","slug":"003-programme"}],"audio":{"filter":{"by_title":["Srila B.S. Govinda Dev-Goswami Maharaj","Srila B.R. Sridhar Dev-Goswami Maharaj","Nabadwip temple","Kamal Krishna Prabhu","Manasa Krishna Prabhu"]}},"songsCount":194},"descriptions":[{"title":"Kirtan Guide","title_full_short":"Kīrtan Guide 12th Ed","subtitle":"London, Twelfth Edition, 2026","slug":"en","sort_order":1,"shortcuts":[{"icon":"clock","title":"The Daily Programme","slug":"003-programme"}],"audio":{"filter":{"by_title":["Srila B.S. Govinda Dev-Goswami Maharaj","Srila B.R. Sridhar Dev-Goswami Maharaj","Nabadwip temple","Kamal Krishna Prabhu","Manasa Krishna Prabhu"]}},"songsCount":194}],"nav":{"72":{"prev":{"path":"/en/bhai-re-shiachira-angane-kabhu/","title":"Nabadwīpe Prasāda-sevana"},"next":{"path":"/en/kobe-shri-chaitanya-more-koribena-daya/","title":"Dainya Prārthanā Gīti"}}},"song":{"meta":{"page":72,"author":"Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur","first_line":"bhāi re! eka-dina nīlāchale prasāda-sevana-kāle","alt_first_lines":"eka-dina nīlāchale prasāda-sevana-kāle"},"title":["Nīlāchale Prasāda-sevana"],"author":["by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["bhāi re!","eka-dina nīlāchale    prasāda-sevana-kāle","    mahāprabhu śrī-kṛṣṇa-chaitanya","balilena bhakta-gaṇe,    “khecharānna śuddha-mane","    sevā kari’ hao āja dhanya"],"translation":["O brother! One day in Nīlāchal at the time of honouring prasādam, Mahāprabhu Śrī Kṛṣṇa Chaitanya said to the devotees, “Be fortunate today by honouring khichuḍi with pure hearts."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["“khecharānna piṭhā-pānā    apūrva prasāda nānā","    jagannātha dila tomā sabe","ākaṇṭha bhojana kari’    bala mukhe hari hari","    avidyā-durita nāhi rabe"],"translation":["“Lord Jagannātha has given you khichuḍi, pancakes, sherbet, and various other types of wonderful prasād. Eat up to your neck and chant the Name of Hari! Ignorance and sin will disappear."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["“jagannātha-prasādānna    viriñchi-śambhura mānya","    khāile prema ha-ibe udaya","emana durlabha dhana    pāiyāchha sarva-jana","    jaya jaya jagannātha jaya”"],"translation":["“Lord Jagannātha’s prasād is honoured by Lord Brahmā and Lord Śiva. If you eat it, divine love will arise within you. You all have now attained such a precious treasure. Glory! Glory! Glory to Lord Jagannātha!”"],"isLong":false}],"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":null},"head":{"canonical":"/en/bhai-re-eka-dina-nilachale-prasada-sevana-kale/","description":"Nīlāchale Prasāda-sevana — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Nīlāchale Prasāda-sevana. by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en","slug":"bhai-re-eka-dina-nilachale-prasada-sevana-kale"}}